  "sourceId": "thinksr",
  "title": "ThinkSR: compact thought, dense output",
  "lang": "en",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s01-flow",
      "intent": "The recurrence returns to the compact thought stage, while the dense carrier continues through the flow.",
      "claim": "ThinkSR end to end: encoder, windows, shared DQ-CTM ticks, decoder.",
      "narration": "The image first becomes a dense carrier, because super-resolution needs spatial detail to survive. Windowing turns that field into local token groups without making the thought state dense. The DQ-CTM stage repeats its thought update with shared parameters across ticks. The loop returns only to the thought process, then decoding produces the final high-resolution image.",
