    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation first builds a dense feature field from the low-resolution image, then partitions that field into windows without dropping tokens.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution input into a dense feature field. That dense field is the carrier the compact thought process reads and updates. Window partitioning forms the token set from the same field, so the spatial carrier is retained.",
